  <p class="identity"><span>Hustle Street</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Privacy Policy</span></p>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: 16 November 2026</p>

  <p>This policy explains what happens to information when you play <strong>Hustle Street</strong> on iPhone or Android. It is written for players aged 10 and up and for their parents.</p>
  <p>Hustle Street is published by <strong>Abren Systems LLC</strong>, a company registered in New Mexico, United States (“we”, “us”). If you have any question, email us at <a href="mailto:support@abrensystems.com">support@abrensystems.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There are no accounts, no sign-up and no login.</li>
    <li>The game shows no ads, uses no advertising IDs, and does not track you across other apps or websites.</li>
    <li>Your saved games and progress stay on your phone or tablet. We never receive them.</li>
    <li>The game doesn’t send gameplay statistics or analytics.</li>
    <li>Information leaves your device only to confirm and restore purchases, and, if you choose, for Game Center or Google Play Games.</li>
    <li>We don’t sell or share personal data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>1. No accounts, no ads, no ad tracking</h2>
  <p>You don’t need to sign up or log in to play. The game shows no ads, uses no advertising IDs, and does not track players across other apps or websites. We don’t sell or share personal data.</p>

  <h2>2. Your game data stays on your device</h2>
  <p>Saved games, your street, profile names you type in the game, your settings and your progress are stored only on your phone or tablet. We never receive them. If you delete the app, they are deleted too.</p>

  <h2>3. Game statistics</h2>
  <p>The App Store and Google Play versions of Hustle Street don’t send gameplay statistics or analytics events to us or to any analytics provider.</p>

  <h2>4. Purchases</h2>
  <p>The core game is free. Hustle Street Plus is one optional, one-time purchase that unlocks extra districts. There are no subscriptions, and nothing is sold during a match.</p>
  <p>Payment is handled entirely by Apple (App Store) or Google (Google Play). We never see card or bank details.</p>
  <p>We use RevenueCat to confirm purchases and restore them. When the game checks or restores a purchase, RevenueCat receives the store’s purchase record and an app user ID that RevenueCat creates at random for your copy of the game. That ID isn’t your name, email or an advertising ID, but it stays the same over time so your purchases can be confirmed and restored. Like any service on the internet, RevenueCat also sees your device’s IP address when the game connects to it.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple’s privacy policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat’s privacy policy</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Game Center and Google Play Games (optional)</h2>
  <p>If you are signed in to Game Center (iOS) or Google Play Games (Android), the game reports the achievements you unlock to that service, under your Apple or Google account. That account and its activity are managed by Apple or Google under their own privacy policies. We don’t receive its details. If you aren’t signed in, nothing is reported.</p>

  <h2>6. Notifications (optional)</h2>
  <p>“A note from the street” is a once-a-day reminder you can turn on in Settings. It is scheduled on your device itself. No data is sent to us.</p>

  <h2>7. Sharing (optional)</h2>
  <p>When you tap Share, your device’s own share sheet sends the image or link you chose to the app you pick. We don’t receive it.</p>
  <p>The game may also show your phone’s own rating prompt. If you rate or review the game, that goes to Apple or Google under their policies.</p>

  <h2>8. Your region</h2>
  <p>The game reads your phone’s region setting, on the device, to choose the seasons on your street. It does not use location services or GPS, and your region is not sent to us.</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>Hustle Street is designed for ages 10 and up. Store age ratings and local restrictions apply separately. The game has no accounts, chat or ads, and it never asks for a name, email, photo or location. Profile names typed in the game stay on the device.</p>
  <p>Information leaves the device only in the ways described above:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>when someone buys or restores a purchase, the store’s purchase record and RevenueCat’s app user ID go to Apple or Google and to RevenueCat (section 4);</li>
    <li>if the player is signed in to Game Center or Google Play Games, achievement unlocks go to that service (section 5).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We use this information only to provide purchases and achievements, never for advertising or profiling.</p>
  <p>Purchases are made through the Apple or Google account on the device, so the account holder controls them. Parents can use the stores’ own family and purchase-approval settings. Parents are welcome to contact us with any question at <a href="mailto:support@abrensystems.com">support@abrensystems.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Your game data is on your device, and deleting the app deletes it. Apple or Google keep their own records of your purchases under their privacy policies.</p>
  <p>To ask about, or ask us to delete, the purchase records RevenueCat holds for us, or for anything else, email <a href="mailto:support@abrensystems.com">support@abrensystems.com</a>. If you live in the EU or the UK, you can also complain to your data protection authority.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If the app’s data practices change, we’ll update this page and the “Last updated” date at the top.</p>

